# Frontend Rules

## Design System

### Colors
```css
--background: #0a0a0a;
--surface: #111111;
--surface-2: #1a1a1a;
--border: #222222;
--amber: #F59E0B;       /* Primary accent — Pretty Fly brand */
--amber-dim: #92400E;
--text: #FAFAFA;
--text-muted: #71717A;
--green: #22C55E;       /* Positive / validated */
--red: #EF4444;         /* Warning / leak */
```

### Typography
- Headings: `font-bold tracking-tight`
- Numbers: `font-mono` (JetBrains Mono via Google Fonts)
- Body: `text-sm text-zinc-400`

### Component Pattern
```tsx
// All cards use this base
<div className="bg-[#111] border border-[#222] rounded-xl p-6">
```

## API Calls
All fetch calls go through `frontend/lib/api.ts`:
```typescript
const API = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL ?? "http://localhost:8000"

export async function getCashLeaks(asOfDate?: string): Promise<CashLeaksResponse> {
  const url = asOfDate ? `${API}/api/cash-leaks?as_of_date=${asOfDate}` : `${API}/api/cash-leaks`
  const res = await fetch(url)
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(await res.text())
  return res.json()
}
```

## State Management
Use Zustand for global app state:
```typescript
interface AppStore {
  isDataLoaded: boolean
  validationStatus: "pending" | "passed" | "failed"
  cashLeaks: CashLeak[]
  totalRecoverable: number
  setDataLoaded: (v: boolean) => void
  // ...
}
```

## Loading States
Every data-fetching component shows a skeleton, not a spinner.
Use `animate-pulse` on placeholder divs.

## Formatting
```typescript
// Always format GBP amounts as:
const fmt = (n: number) => `£${n.toLocaleString("en-GB", { maximumFractionDigits: 0 })}`
// e.g. £18,200
```

## No Form Tags
Never use HTML `<form>`. Use button `onClick` handlers instead.

## Component File Structure
```
components/
├── CashMeter.tsx       # Animated total recoverable amount
├── LeakCard.tsx        # Single cash leak item
├── LeakList.tsx        # Ranked list of LeakCards
├── ReconciliationBadge.tsx
├── BacktestTimeline.tsx
├── EmailPreview.tsx
└── DataLoader.tsx      # Folder path input + validate trigger
```

## Page Structure
Each page:
1. Check `isDataLoaded` from Zustand → if false, redirect to DataLoader
2. Fetch data via `useEffect` + store in local state
3. Show skeleton while loading
4. Show error state if fetch fails

## Key Aesthetic Rules
- Numbers are always large and amber
- Every card has a subtle amber left border on hover
- No rounded corners bigger than `rounded-xl`
- No shadows — use borders for depth
- Dark enough that amber pops
